    "note": "brackets from the drawings on pp. 34 (base simples: CT100-286, CT100-388) and 35 (base dupla: CT100-788, CT100-888): legs 100, holes F at 35 and 90 from the heel on each leg, one row (4x) or two rows A apart (8x). Fits: the double-base page names 40x80, 80x80 and 45x90, and A (40, 45) picks the series; the single-base page names bases 30 to 50 for both, so the split (CT100-286 base 30; CT100-388 bases 40 and 45, base 50 having no system yet) follows the shop's kit names. Fastener sets, one per hole: one of each line of the kit for that base (CT100-286-K30, CT100-388-K4050 and -K45B, CT100-788-K4080, CT100-888-K4590), which is our reading, not the shop's. Union plate PLU40-01 from p. 29: 80 x 30 x 2.5, two slots 7 wide 40 apart with 3 of travel (10 long), across two base 40 bars side by side, so the plate's 80 runs along y and the bars along x; the shop states no fixings"
